  "sources": [
    {
      "url": "https://erfgoed.utrecht.nl/verhalen/domtoren",
      "inspection": "Cityheritage page actually read: firstsquare38.6m, secondsquare29.48m, lantern26m, uppergallery near95m, roof106.75m and gildedStMartin vane112.32mtotal. Brick/multiple naturalstones. Current low timbercap follows redesign, not never-built stone spire.1920svisitor reception is distinct/excluded.2018–2024restoration noted."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://erfgoed.utrecht.nl/verhalen/bouw-van-de-domtoren",
      "inspection": "City construction history actually read: original independent tower/underpass; foundation excavation23×23m/5.5mdeep is foundation-only comparison, not current aboveground width. Eight open lantern piers/short timber roof and stone vault instead of proposed126mtall stone spire. Nave/bridge chapel and historical red-white reconstruction excluded."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://erfgoed.utrecht.nl/verhalen/domtoren/het-uurwerk-van-de-domtoren",
      "inspection": "Cityclock page actually read:four clockfaces meet atKapBeierij~50m, clock mechanism~40m. External clockwork restored2004; interior machinery excluded. Fixed hand angle illustrative, not a running clock/current time."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.domtoren.nl/het-verhaal/restauratie/",
      "inspection": "Operator restoration page actually read: work2019–2024completed9November2024, corroborates dated2024local scaffold-free photograph. Temporary scaffold in2023image/current map aerial not authored."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.nicodebont.nl/projecten/domtoren-utrecht",
      "inspection": "Restoration contractor page actually read: deliveryNovember2024; replaced/repaired stone, rooflead/slate, glass, clocks, bells/vane/cross. Newfine stone/block finish not fully reconstructed from night image; modest pale restrained palette, geometric carvings remain estimates."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://monumentenregister.cultureelerfgoed.nl/node/736226",
      "inspection": "PrimaryRCEsearch result record36075read; directpage cachemiss.Confirms tower1321–1382and20thCrestoredGothic balustrades. No unseen detail inferred from failed page."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.google.com/maps/@52.09065,5.1214,20z/data=!3m1!1e3",
      "inspection": "Map aerial actually inspected. Imagery shows restoration scaffolding of an earlier date, so used only for tower/footprint/site orientation and separate cathedral/visitorreception relationship. Independent map tunnel centerline confirms passage fromServetstraat west toDomplein east, parallel positiveX. Actual current appearance instead grounded in dated2024local photo/operator restoration record."
    }
  ],
